-- title:
--   Geometric integrality of the rational fibre of the two-chart model
-- statement:
--   Let $N$ be a nonzero natural number. Write $F = \mathrm{modularFunctionFieldFull}\ N$ for the intermediate field of the Laurent series field $\mathbb{Q}((q))$ over $\mathbb{Q}$ generated by the set of series $\mathrm{qExpand}\ \mathbb{Q}\ d\ jq$ for the nonzero divisors $d$ of $N$, and let $\mathrm{jFull}\ N \in F$ be the element given by the $q$-expansion $jq$ itself. From the datum $(\mathbb{Z}, F, \mathrm{jFull}\ N)$ the project forms the two-chart integral model [`AlgebraicCurve.TwoChartIntegralModel`](def/AlgebraicCurve_TwoChartIntegralModel.html#L236), the scheme obtained as the pushout of the two morphisms $\mathrm{fFin}$ and $\mathrm{fInf}$ of affine spectra, i.e. the gluing of a finite and an infinite chart along their overlap, together with its structure morphism $\mathrm{toBase}$ to $\operatorname{Spec}\mathbb{Z}$. Its base change to $\mathbb{Q}$ is the fibre product of $\mathrm{toBase}$ with $\operatorname{Spec}$ of $\mathbb{Z} \to \mathbb{Q}$, and `baseChangeToBase` is the second projection of that square, a morphism to $\operatorname{Spec}\mathbb{Q}$. The assertion is that this morphism is geometrically integral in Mathlib's sense: for every field $K$, every morphism $\operatorname{Spec} K \to \operatorname{Spec}\mathbb{Q}$ and every scheme $Z$ completing it to a pullback square over `baseChangeToBase`, the scheme $Z$ is integral.
--
--   This identifies the generic fibre of the two-chart integral model attached to the full modular function field of level $N$ as a geometrically integral $\mathbb{Q}$-scheme, the statement that lets the model play the role of the modular curve $X_0(N)$ over $\mathbb{Q}$. It is used in the project's smoothness-and-integrality package for the Igusa scheme over $\mathbb{Q}$ and in the constructions of the Abel–Jacobi map and of the Hecke-type operators attached to a de Rham model package.
